;(Talk to Yancui)
;(First interaction)
::'''Yancui:''' Hello, guest. Sorry to bother you, but I noticed from your attire that you are an Outworld traveler. Do you have any unique ingredients or recipes that you can tell me about?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't do my own cooking.
:::'''Yancui:''' I see. Sorry for bothering you then.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's all home-cooked fare. Nothing special.
:::'''Yancui:''' Is that so? I guess I'm the one asking a strange question.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Have you heard of interstellar locusts?
:::'''Yancui:''' I've eaten them before... They didn't taste great though. Thanks anyways.
::'''Yancui:''' Ah, I forgot to introduce myself... I am Yancui, head chef and owner of Spices Supreme. The restaurant's not busy right now, so I'm taking a break here in Exalting Sanctum, but couldn't take my mind off developing new dishes.
::'''Yancui:''' Spices Supreme isn't far from here. Please visit us if you're interested. Our motto is to "cook for the people." We guarantee our food is inexpensive and tasty!
::'''Yancui:''' Ah, I've chatted so much with you. Here's something for you to have a taste test. You must come to Spices Supreme to try our dishes if you get a chance! It'll be an experience you'll never forget!
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Yancui:''' Let's have a look then. What shall we have for this week's Odd-taste Thursday... Gizzard sashimi, kidney stew, brown sugar sesame porridge, steamed boar skin, charcoal barbecued black donkey hooves, caramel-drizzled stinky tofu...
::'''Yancui:''' Hmm? You want to discuss food for a little longer? I love to chat about cuisine with people.
;(If {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502014201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Ambrosial Arbor is growing again...
::'''Yancui:''' I was still working back of house then, and all we could hear was the clattering of diners out front.
::'''Yancui:''' I rushed out of the kitchen and watched as the Arbor slowly grew. I had been pretty well-traveled, but I was flabbergasted.
::'''Yancui:''' Just looking at that thing made my skin crawl. It grew at this weird, steady pace as if it were the only tree in all of existence...
::'''Yancui:''' After all these years of boxing, my intuition is still dead-on about this kind of thing... That thing is so packed full of vitality that it could almost raise the dead...
::'''Yancui:''' So... You have to be careful in the future. I'm still waiting for you to come and visit us in-store.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502014201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Finally, the Ambrosial Arbor crisis is behind us...
::'''Yancui:''' Yeah, it's finally over... Even though it hasn't been that long, it feels like we've been going through it for a long time.
::'''Yancui:''' I still remember clearly that scene, when I was in my kitchen and I came out and saw it growing... I've never seen anything so spectacular since it stopped growing.
::'''Yancui:''' This is actually a good thing... A restaurant should feel like a restaurant. Back then, everyone was so troubled and weighed down by their worries that they couldn't even fully enjoy the dishes I had carefully prepared for them.
::'''Yancui:''' ...That was definitely a terrible time... But now, everyone has calmed down, and I feel happy and motivated to see how they enjoy my dishes.
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502014201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Has business been going well lately?
::'''Yancui:''' Thanks to your sponsorship, my business has been going well. A few days ago, my store was even ranked on the "Top 100 Darkest Dishes in the Cosmos" made by Outworlders... Haha.
::'''Yancui:''' My friends were afraid to tell me about it because they thought I'd get angry.... but I'm actually happy!
::'''Yancui:''' Recently, I've been getting a lot of attention from Outworlders who come here just to try my "dark dishes." They even formed a "Dark Cuisine Council" and have been asking me to join as a member!
::'''Yancui:''' I'm glad to have more customers. As for the "Council," however... I hate the idea of chefs grouping together to come up with "industry standards" or something like that, so I've refused their offer.
::'''Yancui:''' Just drop by and enjoy a hearty meal whenever you're free. My store might be busy these days, but I'll always reserve a seat for you!
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502014201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог}} There is something I want to ask you...
::'''Yancui:''' Go ahead. I'll tell you everything I know, as long as they're not business secrets.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Business secrets? Such as?
:::'''Yancui:''' Hmm? I was just saying that! I don't think I have anything you'd call a business secret...
:::'''Yancui:''' You might laugh at us, but we Xianzhou chefs are very careful about our recipes being leaked to the public. Some of our most common cooking methods have even been mystified...
:::'''Yancui:''' For example, slicing tofu into thin threads as fine as silk... At the end of the day, it's just putting in the time and effort and learning through mistakes.
:::'''Yancui:''' But spoken from a chef's perspective, it becomes all about the "power in the wrists," "artful skill," "unfathomable secret" &mdash; all these pretentious big words that confuse people... Even I'm left scratching my head.
:::'''Yancui:''' Spices Supreme employs no such tactics. If you really want to know how a dish is made, I'll even give you a step-by-step. Doesn't matter if you don't get it the first time: Just look up "Spices Supreme Yancui" online and my recipes' videos are all there.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Do you have any recommendations?
:::'''Yancui:''' You can try our trademark dishes like the crisped melon and diced chicken, pork slices in fish sauce, and Granny Chen's Tofu to start. These are all famous dishes that have withstood the test of time. You can't go wrong with them.
:::'''Yancui:''' Everyone's tastes are different, and my recommendations might not suit your palate. But we've got myriads of flavors, so I'm sure there's one that'll pique your fancy.
:::'''Yancui:''' You know that a Xianzhou native's life is long, so they are very particular about variety in their pursuit of flavor.
:::'''Yancui:''' Every Thursday, we've got an "Odd-taste Thursday" event, where we serve some dishes with rather interesting flavors. It's to provide some variety and fun for Xianzhou gormandizers.
:::'''Yancui:''' These new dishes may not be tasty, but they'll definitely leave you with an unforgettable experience.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What's your favorite dish?
:::'''Yancui:''' I'm ashamed to admit that though I run a restaurant, I'm actually quite picky about my food. There are some things I don't eat... such as...
:::'''Yancui:''' Such as animals who can't defeat me &mdash; I'll never eat those!
:::'''Yancui:''' We Vidyadhara have always observed the law of natural flow. All creatures are connected to one another, and life is everlasting in its cycle. Based on this principle, if an animal can't defeat me on even ground, I'd never use it as food! That is my martial way!
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What exactly are you talking about...
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What's the logic behind this?
:::'''Yancui:''' C'mon, that's where you're ignorant! I may look like a pushover, but I am the Cloudbanner Meteor Fist's chief disciple. My fists are unrivaled among the auxiliary martial art schools in Xianzhou!
:::'''Yancui:''' It's just that I went into the food business in the end, so I didn't take over the martial art school. But I've still retained the pride of a martial artist, heehee.
:::'''Yancui:''' I don't eat small fish and shrimp, nor herbivores, or even domesticated beasts... I only eat animals that I can fight to the death with.
:::'''Yancui:''' Of course, that's just my personal mantra. Spices Supreme serves everything. Don't worry.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So... what's your favorite dish?
::::'''Yancui:''' Oh, I completely forgot your question! We Vidyadhara can't reproduce naturally, so the Sky-Faring Commission's travel reviewers are fairly lenient, which means I've had many opportunities to hunt on other worlds.
::::'''Yancui:''' Some worlds teem with numerous ferocious beasts... My most vivid memory was of an ocean world called Thalassa...
::::'''Yancui:''' It had a giant airborne beast called a six-eyed flying fish. I stood on it, and we were locked in battle for hours. It was a miracle it didn't swallow me whole!
::::'''Yancui:''' The fins of that fish were delicious beyond compare! That fin stew was the tastiest dish I'd ever had...
::::'''Yancui:''' Apart from that, I also like deep-fried flying sea anemone, fruitwood-grilled Shantak moa drumettes, viscorpus sugar balls stir-fried with cured meat... Oh right, these viscorpi may be really tiny, but they sure can conjure horrifying hallucinations. What a ride...
::::'''Yancui:''' Haha, sorry, very few people ask me about my ingredient-seeking escapades, and I got carried away.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Is... Is that so...? Amazing...
::::'''Yancui:''' Heheh, I am quite amazing! Not just at martial arts, but cooking too. You must try my food out!
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Spices Supreme...
:::'''Yancui:''' You're wondering why I opened this restaurant? Well, it's a long story...
:::'''Yancui:''' The IPC had this subsidiary company a hundred years ago which sold conveyor belts, and they had an "Interastral Gourmet Association" that went around and rated all the eateries throughout the whole cosmos.
:::'''Yancui:''' If you get one star, you're part of the "Interastral Selection." If you get five stars, then you're the "Cosmos's Finest Diner." Across all of the Xianzhou ships, the only place to ever get five stars from them is "Dragon Palace's Kitchen" on the Xianzhou Zhuming.
:::'''Yancui:''' Being Vidyadhara, I thought I had to go and support the business of my kin, especially when they received such honors... But that place charged hundreds of thousands of credits for portions that won't even be filling for little birds! Would you believe it?
:::'''Yancui:''' That chef even put on this pretentious air and told Outworlders, "We Vidyadhara are indifferent to the trappings of fame and fortune, which is why we eat like this." Ack, that was too much...
:::'''Yancui:''' That's when I determined to run a restaurant that goes completely opposite to everything they stood for. I want big portions, quality food, and low prices! I'm telling ya, Spices Supreme is that dream come true!
:::'''Yancui:''' But to be honest, if you hadn't mentioned it today, I'd have forgotten about that goal... Now I run the restaurant just to have fun. Nothing else.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} I'll come back later...
:::'''Yancui:''' Fine. Not to worry. Any time! Can't wait! Take care! Stay safe out there!
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502014201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I'll come back later...
::'''Yancui:''' Fine. Not to worry. Any time! Can't wait! Take care! Stay safe out there!

;(Talk to Lianyan)
;(First interaction)
::'''Lianyan:''' Toys, doorbells, flexible displays!~ Shelves, refrigerators, extractor fans!~ Starskiffs, jade abaci, massage chairs!~ Second hand, or broken, I buy them all!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What song are you singing?
:::'''Lianyan:''' ...Singing? Oh... I'm not singing. I'm hawking for business!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} (Clapping in rhythm)
:::'''Lianyan:''' Toys, doorbells... Wait, don't just clap along. I'm hawking for business. If you clap like that, people will think it's a street show.
::'''Lianyan:''' Oh yeah, by the way &mdash; I'm Lianyan, manager at the Oldies Depot. And when I say manager, I mean I'm the only person there. It's just me and my small business.
::'''Lianyan:''' The Oldies Depot mainly buys and sells second-hand appliances, fixes up old stuff, and buys antiques. But Xianzhou people live so long that they have no interest in anything old, let alone bothering to fix anything...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So you buy trashed items?
:::'''Lianyan:''' ...It's just a title. Call it whatever you want.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do the Xianzhou people only like new things?
:::'''Lianyan:''' Not quite... But most of the regulars here are Outworlders. Sometimes we'll get a Xianzhou shopper selling some junk to make a little pocket money, but never anyone buying second-hand goods or repairing things.
::'''Lianyan:''' You don't seem to have anything old there that needs fixing. Don't tell me you've come for a chat?
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Lianyan:''' Toys, doorbells, mirrors!~ Starskiffs, jade abaci, massage chairs!~ Second hand, or broken, I buy them all!
::'''Lianyan:''' Oh hey, you're back. Got something for me to fix? Or just a casual catch-up?
;(If {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502015201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Ambrosial Arbor is growing again...
::'''Lianyan:''' I saw, and even tried going to nearby Scalegorge Waterscape to rubberneck, but the Cloud Knights sent me back, haha.
::'''Lianyan:''' The Arbor's growth isn't actually a good thing... But let's talk somewhere more private... I love how beautiful the Ambrosial Arbor looks.
::'''Lianyan:''' But only how it looks! I've studied my history and this is not a good thing.
::'''Lianyan:''' But I can't help it. I guess I was just born with a love for majestic landscapes like this.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502015201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Ambrosial Arbor has stopped growing...
::'''Lianyan:''' Yeah, that's hardly news to me. As soon as I heard about it, I went there and checked it out myself, and I saw from Exalting Sanctum with my own eyes that it had stopped growing.
::'''Lianyan:''' Well... I'll tell you a secret, but don't tell anyone, okay? Otherwise I might end up in hot water with the Realm-Keeping Commission... Some curio sellers were using the Ambrosial Arbor's sprouting as a gimmick to attract customers.
::'''Lianyan:''' Just so you know, they were claiming that their curios were influenced by the anomaly or even came from the Ambrosial Arbor itself. But don't fall for their tricks, okay?
::'''Lianyan:''' Now that the Ambrosial Arbor has stopped growing, I've seen an opportunity and acquired those curios at incredibly low prices. To my surprise, some of them are actually pretty interesting and not just cheap gimmicks like I thought they would be. A pleasant surprise, don't you agree?
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502015201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Has business been going well lately?
::'''Lianyan:''' It's been amazing! Aurum Alley never used to have any travelers, and I only ever did business with Xianzhou locals... But, well, you know how the Xianzhou folks are like... They don't really need my services.
::'''Lianyan:''' But everything has changed, now! The Aurum Alley is full of outworlders and they love the ancient "artifacts" of Xianzhou.
::'''Lianyan:''' These outworlders value artifacts differently to us, so my friends keep telling me to up the prices but... well, it's just old stuff, isn't it?
::'''Lianyan:''' I've never dreamed of becoming rich in this life. I have just one simple wish: "to make the best use of everything." That is all.
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502015201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог}} That's right. I just want to chat...
::'''Lianyan:''' Really? How curious... What do you want to chat about?
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What's the Oldies Depot about?
:::'''Lianyan:''' My teacher used to run it, but he handed over everything to me since it was almost time for him to undergo his hatching rebirth. I never cared for this place in the slightest, to begin with.
:::'''Lianyan:''' My master used to be so darn strict. A man of very few words, only smiling when he was handling antique items. If you ask him, renovating something old is the most amazing pursuit there could ever be.
:::'''Lianyan:''' But these Xianzhou people live on and on, just like stagnant water. Yet all the stuff aboard Xianzhou metabolizes super-fast &mdash; like bugs in that stagnant water, flailing about fleetingly.
:::'''Lianyan:''' He always said, "Heaven makes no useless people, and the world makes no useless things." Meaning that, nothing and nobody is ever truly a waste.
:::'''Lianyan:''' So this little Oldies Depot is a place for people's keepsakes and old things. There's always gonna be something irreplaceable that needs fixing up.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why don't the Xianzhou people like to repair old things?
:::'''Lianyan:''' There are hardly any heirlooms aboard Xianzhou... Or to put it another way, heirlooms aren't everyday items. Items used every day would never keep up with the long-lived Xianzhou people.
:::'''Lianyan:''' Forget about all the hot new tech that comes out every week. Even mundane stuff like pots and pans rarely last forever. Fixing things takes effort.
:::'''Lianyan:''' And their state of disrepair often requires great skill and a high price to get it fixed... Simply put, repairs are not cheap, and buying something new works out cheaper and more convenient.
:::'''Lianyan:''' That's why it raises eyebrows whenever Outworlders see an antique from centuries ago get discarded without a thought, and being taken in by us as "trash."
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What made you take up this line of business?
:::'''Lianyan:''' Do you like traveling? I do. I got through all the paperwork and went to this tourist resort off Xianzhou called Insumousu.
:::'''Lianyan:''' The people of Insumousu are special indeed. From their birth until their teenage years, they live on land and breathe with their lungs. But once they reach adulthood, they start to live in water and breathe using gills.
:::'''Lianyan:''' Back during the Iron Age, when civilization had barely begun, the people of Insumousu constructed magnificent buildings on the sea floor. Right in the middle of them is a huge statue, rising up out of the sea and stretching into the sky.
:::'''Lianyan:''' Every Insumousu local I met lit up in excitement whenever they mentioned that great ruin. They tell me how it's a totem for their civilization, one that records the noble histories of their great people...
:::'''Lianyan:''' I later found out that the ruins were actually just four hundred years old.
:::'''Lianyan:''' In other words, all the time spent by the great ancestors of Insumousu to build this "totem of civilization" was far shorter than my entire life.
:::'''Lianyan:''' ...I don't mean to talk down on the Insumousu civilization. Their underwater ruins are exquisite and truly magnificent... It's something that is both younger than me, yet has far more gravity than my life.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} That's all. I can see you're busy.
:::'''Lianyan:''' Alright, catch you next time then. If you ever need anything fixed, or if you want to buy and sell second-hand stuff, come find me.
;(If {{Mission|Back in Business (IV)|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed, and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502015201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} That's all. I can see you're busy.
::'''Lianyan:''' Alright, catch you next time then. If you ever need anything fixed, or if you want to buy and sell second-hand stuff, come find me.

;(Talk to Yinshu)
;(First interaction)
::'''Yinshu:''' ...This is a bookstore. If you want to read or pick out a book, just go in and browse around. Call me when you want to pay.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Got anything you can recommend?
:::'''Yinshu:''' I don't really read that much, so I can't really recommend anything... Well, the front of the shop is where we keep our bestsellers. There's gotta be a reason why they're bestsellers. Why not start there?
:::'''Yinshu:''' "Views of the Universe from a Starskiff" is a record of wondrous exoplanets by a foxian explorer... Oh, you're from an exoplanet anyways. In that case, hang on and let me think...
:::'''Yinshu:''' How about this one here, "Otherworldly Delights"? It's a collection of short supernatural stories written by the boss here.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Boss, you could be a little more enthusiastic.
:::'''Yinshu:''' ...Bookstores are for selling books. Besides, I'm not the boss here. I just help with running a few chores. I'm not in charge of sales here.
:::'''Yinshu:''' But then again, the boss here doesn't really give a darn about business at all. Here... This is a collection of short supernatural stories he's written, called "Otherworldly Delights."
::'''Yinshu:''' I'm a relative of the owner. He likes listening to other people's conversations, saying that it's good inspiration as an author.
::'''Yinshu:''' You may have seen him over in Starskiff Haven. He does storytelling in some teahouse called Sleepless Earl or other, calling himself something like "Mr. Xiyan."
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I may have met him in Starskiff Haven.
:::'''Yinshu:''' He likes getting attention. I'd be truly surprised if you haven't seen him.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why are there storytellers aboard Xianzhou?
:::'''Yinshu:''' Have you seen storytellers on other planets? When you put it like that... I can tell you've probably already seen it before.
:::'''Yinshu:''' All I know is, storytelling is a traditional form of performative art. I don't know much else. But perhaps the boss is using his gig as a storyteller to hang out at the teahouse and hear all kinds of supernatural and weird tales.
::'''Yinshu:''' How I wish he could pay a little more attention to his bookstore business... Ah well. Have you got any books there that you'd like to buy?
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Yinshu:''' You pay, then pick out the "bookmark" you like, hold them close to your jade abacus, and download them to read later.
::'''Yinshu:''' If you don't have a jade abacus or if you just like the feeling of a book in your hands, just grab one off the shelf. Scroll rolls, bound bamboo strips, printed and bound paper books &mdash; we've got all the formats. Anyway, just come see me if you'd like to buy a book.
:{{Диалог|Магазин}} I'd like to buy a book.
:{{Диалог}} I'd like to chat with you some more.
::'''Yinshu:''' Okay. Well, as you can see, I've nothing to do, so let's chat.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About supernatural tales aboard the Xianzhou...
:::'''Yinshu:''' The boss here is obsessed with all the supernatural stories told on this ship, and even pays through the nose to make visits to other Xianzhou ships. He never really finds anything, but he has fun along the way.
:::'''Yinshu:''' In fact, most of these stories are just due to otherworldly species or mere coincidence. The Xianzhou people aren't really flustered by any of that, and barely raise an eyebrow.
:::'''Yinshu:''' But the boss says that no matter how brilliant this world is, people always need to have dark and ghostly stories.
:::'''Yinshu:''' "Reality isn't interesting, and what's interesting isn't real. Adding flourish is normal, and vagueness adds flavor." He's got this phrase etched onto his belt.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About recent bestsellers...
:::'''Yinshu:''' There's a new suspense novel out that's very popular, but I haven't read it yet, so can't go over the exact details. But if you're interested in such stories, just buy it and you'll know for sure.
:::'''Yinshu:''' On Xianzhou, we have immortal people, novel technology, and fantastical visitors from exoplanets... But somehow everyone wants to read about primitive crimes conducted in snowbound manor houses with no Cloud Knights, no technology, and no super powers...
:::'''Yinshu:''' I don't really get it. Perhaps that's the charm of mystery novels?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} The appearance of books on Xianzhou all seem kind of retro...
:::'''Yinshu:''' Ah yes, tourists often make this remark.
:::'''Yinshu:''' In fact, if you want, you can take the corresponding "bookmark" you like from the books, hold them close to your jade abacus, and download them to read later.
:::'''Yinshu:''' I personally like downloading and reading off my jade abacus, but there's always people who like the feeling of holding paper books in their hands. The longer people live, the more they crave this kind of ceremony.
:::'''Yinshu:''' Tsk, these physical books are such a pain. They take up space and need daily cleaning.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} I'll be back next time.
:::'''Yinshu:''' Away you go, then. Take care.
;(If {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502016201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Ambrosial Arbor is growing again...
::'''Yinshu:''' *sigh*
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What's with all the sighing?
::'''Yinshu:''' You are the twenty-seventh person to mention this to me today.
::'''Yinshu:''' I see, I see... Mr. Xiyan would probably be interested in this.
::'''Yinshu:''' But I'm just a kid helping out here. Hope this thing doesn't impact my work...
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502016201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Finally, the Ambrosial Arbor crisis is over... What's your take?
::'''Yinshu:''' Alright! Alright! Just stop with all the Ambrosial Arbor stuff!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You didn't answer my question...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Wh&mdash;What's the rush?
::'''Yinshu:''' There have been 52 people who came to talk to me about this matter. Among them, 48 asked me whether there were readables that discussed the secrets behind the growth and ceasing of the Ambrosial Arbor.
::'''Yinshu:''' As a mere bookstore assistant, I have no say in the writing and publishing of readables... Alas... They should pester those editors instead. Anyway, I have no stock of those readables here.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed and {{Mission|Wood Sprouts Anew, Fate Tilts Askew|showChapter=0}} has been completed, {{cx}}<!--performance 502016201 has been seen-->, and {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has not been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I'll be back next time.
::'''Yinshu:''' Away you go, then. Take care.
;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 202030714-->)
:{{Диалог|undefined}} Interact
::'''Yinshu:''' Where did Yunshen get to, I asked him to watch the shop while I used my voucher... He's often hanging around here &mdash; always seemed nice enough. *sigh* Not trustworthy after all.
::'''March 7th:''' That crook wanted to cheat us out of 500 strales.
::'''Yinshu:''' What? You didn't give him the money, did you?
::'''March 7th:''' Of course not! We scared him off.
::'''Yinshu:''' You two are incredible. I'll have to have a word with him later... Ugh, asking him to help was my mistake &mdash; I apologize.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No worries! You weren't to know.
